{"id":"word:hebrew:H859","type":"word","title":"אַתָּה","subtitle":"H859 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"thou and thee , or (plural) ye and you","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אַתָּה (H859) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: p.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 1104 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אַתָּה (ʼattâh) means thou and thee , or (plural) ye and you First listed occurrence: 1Chr 11 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אַתָּה","transliteration":"ʼattâh","pronunciation":"at-taw'","strong":"H859","lemmaId":"hebrew:H859","partOfSpeech":"p","forms":["אַתָּ֣ה","אַתָּ֖ה","אַתָּ֥ה","אַתָּה֙","וְ/אַתָּ֣ה"],"morphs":[["HPp2ms",540],["HPp2mp",213],["HC/Pp2ms",199],["HC/Pp2mp",69],["HPp2fs",49],["HC/Pp2fs",17],["HTi/Pp2ms",10],["HC/Pp2fp",4],["HPp2fp",1],["HTr/Pp2ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"thou and thee , or (plural) ye and you","usage":"thee, thou, ye, you.","full":"H859. attah אָ֑תָּה אַתָּ֫ה, (so regularly; but 26-7 t., with different disjunctive accents, ׃אַ֑תָּה see Fr MM 228 ; Sta § 178 a (read 8 for 18) pronoun 2 singular masculine thou (for anta , see above; compare נָתַתָּ for נָתַנְתָּ ) Gen 3:11 , 19 +? אַתָּ 1Sam 24:19 ; Psa 6:4 ; Job 1:10 ; Eccl 7:22 ; Neh 9:6 . Appended to a verb for emphasis, Exod 18:19 (twice in verse); 1Sam 17:56 אַתָּה שְׁאַל inquire thou , 20:8 ; 22:18 ; Isa 43:26 אַתָּה סַמֵּר . Added for the purpose of strengthening a Genitive or accusative suffix 1Kin 21:19 ; Prov 22:19 (Ges § 135 .2). אתי , i.e. אַתִּי , the older & more original form of אַתְּ thou (feminine), preserved, probably dialectically, 7 t. in Kt, Judg 17:2 ; 1Kin 14:2 ; 2Kin 4:16 , 23 ; 8:1 ; Jer 4:30 ; Ezek 36:13 . (V. above as in Syriac, the י may not have been fully sounded: the Masoretes direct אַתְּ to be everywhere read.) אָ֑תְּ אַתְּ, pronoun 2 singular feminine thou (feminine) (shortened from אַתִּי (q. v.); in Syriac the two Genders are written differently, , , but, the not being sounded, are pronounced alike: in ᵑ7 both are written אַתְּ or אַנְתְּ ) Gen 12:11 , 13 ; 24:23 +? Num 11:15 ; Deut 5:24 ; Ezek 28:14 used as a masculine (as in Aramaic of ᵑ7 ); but probably אַתָּ (see below אַתָּה ) should be here read. אַתֶּם pronoun 2 masculine plural you (masculine) (for antem , see above) Gen 9:7 ; 26:27 ; 29:4 +? הָאַתֶּם הֲ, Judg 6:31 ; following the verb for emphasis 15:12 ; Jer 34:15 ; construed inaccurately with a feminine Ezek 13:20 . אַתֵּן Ezek 34:31 (many editions אַתֶּן ), אַתֵּ֫נָה Gen 31:6 ; Ezek 13:11 , 20 (editions אַתֵּ֫נָּה ) 34:17 pronoun 2 feminine plural you (feminine) I. אסה (perhaps compare Arabic heal , Aramaic אֲסָא , ).","rootNote":"or (shortened); אַתָּ ; or אַת ; feminine (irregular) sometimes אַתִּי ; plural masculine אַתֶּם ; feminine אַתֶּן ; or אַתֵּנָה lemma אתֵּנָה missing vowel, corrected to אַתֵּנָה ; or אַתֵּנָּה ; a primitive pronoun of the second person;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 11 2","keyReferences":["1Chr 11 2","1Chr 11 2","1Chr 11 2","1Chr 15 12","1Chr 15 12","1Chr 15 13","1Chr 17 4","1Chr 17 18"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":1104,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 11 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַתָּ֛ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HPp2ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 11 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַתָּ֨ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HPp2ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 11 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אַתָּה֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Pp2ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 15 12","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַתֶּ֛ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HPp2mp"},{"reference":"1Chr 15 12","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַתֶּ֣ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HP